{"name":"Sunday Afternoon","hex":"#f6c778","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"afternoon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of the day from noon or lunchtime until sunset, evening, or suppertime or 6pm.","The later part of anything, often with implications of decline."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In the afternoon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afternoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aaron Lines","blocks":[{"text":"Anthony Aaron Lines is a Canadian country music singer. He has recorded for RCA Nashville, BNA and On Ramp Records, and has charted three singles on the Hot Country Songs charts in the United States, in addition to landing one number one hit on the Canada Country chart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Aaron_Lines_at_Maverick_Saloon.jpg/330px-Aaron_Lines_at_Maverick_Saloon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_Lines"},{"title":"Sunday","blocks":[{"text":"Sunday is the day of the week between Saturday and Monday. Sunday is a day of rest in most Western countries and a part of the weekend. In some Arab countries, Sunday is a weekday."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunday"},{"title":"Afternoon","blocks":[{"text":"Afternoon is the period from noon to sunset or evening. It is the time when the sun is descending from its peak in the sky to somewhat before its terminus at the horizon in the west. In human life, it occupies roughly the latter half of the standard work and school day. In literal terms, it refers to a time specifically after noon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Wien_T%C3%BCrke